Build a finite offered catalog from the authorized repository context and the original question. Dispatch operation interpret_retrieval_needs through the registered host capability before planning evidence categories or selecting an operation. One host packet carries all five dimensions; the packet references its actual input artifact.

original_question carries the unchanged question. catalog explains the offered meanings. known_ids and context are candidates, not selected targets or authority. source_scope echoes the trusted repository/source policy for identity checks; it does not authorize extra reads. The existing kernel Scope and permissions remain authoritative.

This step applies only to the configured graph-source question path without explicit answer_requirements. A disabled host returns an explicit unresolved result. The kernel's normal wait, ledger and budget owners remain in control. [Preparation adapter](integrations/research_needs.py) and [research continuation](kernel/capabilities/research/needs.py).

The example is an illustrative subset of offered meanings, not a captured production packet or a live-model result.

