Run the selected operation against the pinned generation, then disclose only the evidence allowed by the request and budgets.

Parameters remain scoped; query versions/digests are checked. Results carry source locators and limitations. Dedicated population operations support AC descendants and declared dependents. Fanout, result, excerpt and cumulative continuation limits can make a response partial. Semantic/hybrid mechanisms exist, but require matching embeddings and an approved, ready source mapping; mechanism availability is not production readiness. [Neutral service](knowledge/service.py) · [Answer reference](docs/reference/knowledge-retrieval-answers.md).

I/O boundary: Actual neutral request/result boundary. The illustrative evidence contains one AC excerpt with a missing required field, so it remains partial.

Example boundary: This walkthrough returns one illustrative AC excerpt and a missing test_required field, so status stays partial. It is a documentation example, not actual KM-500c-2 source text or a retrieval receipt.

Explicitly requested test_spec is read only at source disclosure level 3 through
knowledge/requested_fields.py. The source repository, revision, path and file
hash remain pinned. field_contents holds the exact additional YAML span;
field_locators identifies /test_spec and field_availability distinguishes present,
unknown, disclosure_omitted and truncated. This does not change the graph mapper
or disclose arbitrary unrequested fields.

The public adapter creates a separate Evidence excerpt with
source.section_locator=/test_spec and the same source.source_version.commit.
Canonical /criteria stays separate. Additional source bytes and public citations
consume the existing content, evidence-count and shared character budgets;
missing or trimmed disclosure remains partial. The illustrative supplementary
example below demonstrates the output shape only, not a new success receipt.

